 "claim": "No value-free four-place knot is mutually selecting on 4-regular systems, unless NP-complete problems are polynomial: parity fails recognisably but its count is polynomial (2^(n-r) or 0), and its failures are local; the not-exactly-two and twelve classes have coNP-complete failures (C); not-all-equal never fails (B). With B for every k >= 4, the value-free not-all-equal law fails on regular systems only at three places, where its failures are the knot's Pfaffian spaces. So among value-free laws, mutual selection is special to three places. Open: four-place laws that prefer a value, and the counts of the four-place laws.",
